# Copy to .env.local, which git ignores. Vite reads VITE_ variables at build time.
#
# Guests sign in through Better Auth in the API, on the SPA's own origin (/api/auth/*). There is no switch.
# Run the API too (`pnpm dev` at the repo root starts both) with BETTER_AUTH_URL set to this dev server's origin,
# for example http://localhost:4200 (api/.env.example).
#
# Until the account, orders and checkout features move to the API (later stories), those screens read demo data
# kept in this browser, and every signed-in user sees the one demo guest's data. Signing out clears it.

# Read by vite.config.ts, not by the browser. Where the dev server and `vite preview` send /api.
# The API's PORT default is 3000.
# API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:3000
